# 5 Mistakes When Buying a Three Stone Radiant Cut Engagement Ring

Most buyers who want a three stone radiant cut engagement ring picture round brilliant side stones. That combination sells everywhere. It's also mistake number one — and once you see why, you won't be able to unsee it.

The radiant cut is a rectangular diamond. Its shape has long edges, short edges, and cropped corners.

Round side stones have no edges at all. They sit beside the radiant like two circles beside a rectangle.

This guide covers all five mistakes, the right side stone choices — baguette, trapezoid, and half-moon — with certified market pricing across 6 settings, and a full comparison across all metals. Every price is stone plus setting combined.

