The bezel holds each baguette inside a complete metal rim — no prong tips exposed, no catch points for fabric. This is the safest side stone configuration for daily wear. Prong-set side stones in three-stone rings catch on hair and knitwear; bezel-set stones don't.

The baguette shape follows The Shape Echo Rule perfectly. Straight baguettes run parallel to the radiant's long edges.

From above, the ring reads as three rectangles in a line — the center stone largest, the baguettes flanking it symmetrically. It's the cleanest three-stone geometry possible with a radiant center.

The same design is available in [14K Yellow Gold (item 316319)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/bezel-straight-baguette-cut-diamond-three-stone-engagement-ring-in-14k-yellow-gold-by-james-allen-item-316319?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) at $3,030 and in [Platinum (item 316317)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/bezel-straight-baguette-cut-diamond-three-stone-engagement-ring-in-platinum-by-james-allen-item-316317?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) at $3,325. Platinum adds durability at $255 extra — worth it for natural stone buyers expecting to wear the ring for 30+ years.

## Half-Moon Side Stones — The Modern Pick

The [Three-Stone Half-Moon Sidestone in 14K White Gold (item 203679)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/three-stone-half-moon-sidestone-diamond-engagement-ring-in-14k-white-gold-1-2-ct-tw-item-203679?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) at 1/2 ct tw is the most reviewed setting in this guide with 26 ratings — the highest of any three-stone radiant setting in this price range.

[![Three-stone radiant cut engagement ring in yellow gold — shop Blue Nile three stone rings](/images/three-stone-radiant-cut-engagement-ring-yellow-gold.avif)](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings?styleIDs=three_stone&ShapeID=Radiant&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)

A half-moon stone has a flat straight edge and a curved outer edge. The flat edge sits directly against the radiant's corner prong, keeping the stones close together.

The curved outer edge flows into the shank. The result is a three-stone ring that looks softer and more organic than a baguette ring, without using round stones that violate The Shape Echo Rule.

At 1/2 ct tw, the half-moon side stones satisfy The 25% Carat Rule comfortably for center stones between 1ct and 1.75ct. For a 1.5ct radiant center with 1/2 ct tw half-moon sides, the total diamond weight is 2ct — but the center stone clearly leads. The half-moons frame without competing.

